  <div class="legal-page">
    <h1>FTC Disclosure</h1>
    <div class="legal-meta">Last updated: Q2 2026</div>

    <p><strong>TRT Compass participates in affiliate programs.</strong> When you click a link on our site and purchase from a reviewed clinic, we may earn a commission. This does not cost you anything — affiliate fees are paid by the clinic, not the customer.</p>

    <h2>What this means for you</h2>
    <p>We want to be explicit about how this works so you can make an informed decision:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Affiliate links are identified with <code>sponsored</code> or <code>affiliate</code> rel attributes in the HTML.</li>
      <li>Affiliate relationships are disclosed on every page that contains a commission-generating link.</li>
      <li>Our scores and verdicts are determined by merit — a clinic does not pay to appear higher, and a clinic does not pay to remove a negative finding.</li>
      <li>We have never accepted payment in exchange for a favorable review, and we will not.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How affiliate revenue works</h2>
    <p>When you click a clinic link on TRT Compass and purchase a subscription, the clinic tracks that you came from TRT Compass and pays us a commission — typically 10–30% of your first monthly payment. This is standard practice for online health services. The price you pay is identical whether you come through our link or go directly.</p>

    <h2>Incentive alignment</h2>
    <p>Our revenue depends on you being satisfied with your purchase. If we recommend a clinic that delivers poor service, you won't return, and we won't earn from future referrals. This creates a direct alignment between our financial interests and your actual outcome — which is why we take our editorial process seriously.</p>

    <h2>If a clinic changes</h2>
    <p>If a clinic we recommend raises prices, degrades quality, or changes its terms, we update the review in the next quarterly cycle. If a change is significant enough to affect our verdict, we may update immediately. Historical versions of reviews are not archived with timestamps.</p>

    <h2>Questions?</h2>
    <p>If you have questions about our affiliate relationships, contact us at <strong>editorial@trtcompass.com</strong>.</p>

    <div style="margin-top:3rem;padding:1.5rem;background:var(--parchment-dark);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--muted);">
      This disclosure is made in compliance with the FTC's 16 CFR Part 255 guidelines regarding use of endorsements and testimonials in advertising.
    </div>
  </div>

